SubtitleStudio SKIN-4 R6 Android waveform crash containment | 2026-10-16

Device evidence: Android 14 OnePlus CPH2381 (360dp), video pane height
177.2dp with a fixed 180dp waveform plus divider; Flutter reported 3.8dp
bottom RenderFlex overflow at edit_responsive_layout.dart:363 (twice).
Then large legacy PCM cache 330,198,104 samples (~660MB PCM) was read and
25 eager zoom levels generated, followed by device connection loss. The log
does not establish an AndroidRuntime native exception or definite OOM.
Correct both bounded layout and high-memory loading paths.

- Vertical ResizableSplitView accepts minimum first-pane logical extent;
  clamps persisted 0.25 ratio for waveform visibility in live constraints
  and during drag without overwriting saved ratio on mere appearance.
- AdaptiveWaveformPane keeps >=120dp video, caps 180dp waveform, and
  suppresses non-fitting waveform rendering in very short viewports.
- Android AudioProcessor defaults to compact tiled waveform pipeline; other
  platforms retain legacy default and explicit useTiledZoom overrides.
- Upgrade existing same-source PCM cache by streaming WaveformPeakCache.build
  to .pk1 without readAsBytes 660MB and without an FFmpeg second decode.
- Test previous exact 177.2dp layout, .25486577 persisted ratio, short
  viewport and existing waveform peak/tiling parity; flutter analyze and
  full suite. No native phone test in CI; Android acceptance separately.
